## 🔄 Complete Request Flow Diagram

```
User (Postman/Frontend)
        │
        │  POST /api/auth/login  (Body: {email, name, image})
        ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  1. index.ts        │  ← Server receive karta hai request
│  app.use("/api/auth")│  ← Route match karta hai
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  2. routes/auth.ts  │  ← router.post("/login", loginUser)
│  Decide: kis        │     Ye decide karta hai ki request
│  controller ko de   │     kis function ko jayegi
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  3. trycatch.ts     │  ← TryCatch wrapper error pakadta hai
│  (Middleware)       │     Agar controller crash ho toh
│                     │     500 error bhejta hai client ko
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  4. controllers/    │  ← loginUser() ya addUserRole()
│     auth.ts         │     Actual kaam yahan hota hai
│  (Business Logic)   │     DB query, JWT token banana, etc.
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  5. model/User.ts   │  ← Mongoose Model se DB me CRUD
│  (Database Layer)   │     findOne(), create(), findByIdAndUpdate()
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
    MongoDB Atlas
    (Cloud Database)
```

### 🔒 Protected Route Flow (Role Assign):
```
PUT /api/auth/add/role  (Header: "bearer <token>", Body: {role: "seller"})
        │
        ▼
  routes/auth.ts → isAuth (middleware) → addUserRole (controller)
        │                │                      │
        │          Token verify            Role validate
        │          User extract            DB update
        │          req.user set            New token generate
        ▼                ▼                      ▼
     Response: { user: {...}, token: "..." }
```

