## 📝 File-by-File Code Explanation

---

### 1️⃣ [index.ts](file:///c:/Users/rajni/mobigo/services/auth/src/index.ts) — Server ka Entry Point 🚀

```typescript
import express, { urlencoded } from "express";
// ^ Express framework import. urlencoded body parser bhi saath me.

import dotenv from "dotenv";
// ^ .env file ke secrets (PORT, DB URL) ko process.env me load karta hai

import connectDB from "./config/db.js";
// ^ DB connection function import. ⚠️ .js extension lagana zaruri hai
// Kyunki TypeScript compile hoke JS banta hai, runtime pe .js hi chalta hai

import authRoutes from "./routes/auth.js";
// ^ Auth ke saare routes import

dotenv.config();
// ^ .env file padho aur process.env me daal do
// Ab process.env.PORT = "5000", process.env.MONGODB_URI = "mongodb+srv://..."

const app = express();
// ^ Express application ka instance banaya. Ye humare server ka "body" hai.

const PORT = process.env.PORT || 5000;
// ^ .env se PORT lo, agar nahi mila toh default 5000 use karo
// || (OR operator): Left side falsy ho toh right side use karo

app.use(express.json());
// ^ Middleware: Incoming JSON body ko parse karo
// Bina iske req.body = undefined rahega!

app.use(urlencoded({extended:true}));
// ^ Middleware: Form data (x-www-form-urlencoded) ko parse karo

app.use("/api/auth", authRoutes);
// ^ "/api/auth" se start hone wali saari requests authRoutes ko bhejo
// Jaise: POST /api/auth/login → routes/auth.ts handle karega

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${PORT}`);
  connectDB();  // Server start hote hi DB se connect karo
});
```

**🎯 Interview Q:** `app.use()` aur `app.get()` me kya farq hai?
- `app.use()` = Har HTTP method (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) ke liye match karta hai
- `app.get()` = Sirf GET request ke liye match karta hai

