### 2️⃣ [config/db.ts](file:///c:/Users/rajni/mobigo/services/auth/src/config/db.ts) — Database Connection 🗄️

```typescript
import mongoose from "mongoose";
// ^ Mongoose = MongoDB ke liye ODM (Object Data Modeling) library
// Ye JS objects ko MongoDB documents me convert karta hai

const connectDB = async () => {
// ^ async function kyunki DB connect hona ek TIME-TAKING kaam hai
// Network call hai, toh Promise return hoga

    try {
        await mongoose.connect(process.env.MONGODB_URI as string, {
        //                                              ^^^^^^^^
        // 🔥 TYPE ASSERTION: process.env.MONGODB_URI ka type hai
        //    "string | undefined". Par mongoose.connect() ko
        //    sirf "string" chahiye. "as string" se hum TS ko
        //    guarantee de rahe hain: "Bhai ye undefined nahi hoga!"
            dbName: "MobiGO",
            // ^ MongoDB Atlas me "MobiGO" naam ka database use karo
        });
        console.log("MongoDB connected ✅");
    } catch (error) {
        console.log(error);
        // Agar connection fail ho toh error print karo
        // (Wrong URI, network issue, etc.)
    }
}

export default connectDB;
// ^ Ise bahar (index.ts me) import karke use kar sakte hain
```

**🎯 Interview Q:** `async/await` kya hai?
- JS me kuch kaam time lete hain (DB call, API call) = **Asynchronous**
- `async` function me `await` lagane se wo line ka result aane tak **rukta** hai
- Bina await ke code aage badh jayega bina result ke!

