### 3️⃣ [model/User.ts](file:///c:/Users/rajni/mobigo/services/auth/src/model/User.ts) — Data Shape Define karna 👤

```typescript
import mongoose, { Schema, Document } from "mongoose";
// Schema = Database table ka structure define karne ka tool
// Document = Mongoose document ka TypeScript type

export interface IUser extends Document {
// ^ "IUser" = Interface. Ye TypeScript ko batata hai ki ek User me
//   kya kya properties hongi. "I" prefix = Interface convention.
// "extends Document" = Mongoose ki built-in properties bhi inherit karo
//   (jaise _id, __v, save(), etc.)

  name: string;     // User ka naam (sirf string allowed)
  email: string;    // User ka email
  image: string;    // Profile image URL
  role: string;     // User ka role (customer/admin/seller)
}
// 💡 Ye Interface sirf TypeScript ke liye hai, compile hone ke baad
//    ye code GAYAB ho jata hai! Ye sirf "guard" hai.

const schema: Schema<IUser> = new Schema(
// ^ Schema banana = MongoDB ko batana ki data ka structure kya hoga
// Schema<IUser> = Generic. TS ko bata rahe hain ki ye schema
//                 IUser interface follow karega
  {
    name: {
      type: String,       // MongoDB ka String type
      required: true,     // Zaruri hai, bina iske save nahi hoga
    },
    email: {
      type: String,
      required: true,
      unique: true,       // Ek email sirf ek baar aa sakti hai DB me
    },
    image: {
      type: String,
      required: true,
    },
    role: {
      type: String,
      default: null,      // Jab user pehli baar signup kare, role null hoga
    },
  },
  { timestamps: true },
  // ^ Automatically createdAt & updatedAt fields add karega
);

const User = mongoose.model<IUser>("User", schema);
// ^ Ye line actually MongoDB me "users" collection se link karti hai
// mongoose.model("User") → MongoDB me "users" (lowercase + plural) collection
// <IUser> = Generic → Is model se jo bhi data aayega wo IUser type ka hoga

export default User;
// ^ Controller me import karke DB operations (find, create, update) kar sakte hain
```

**🎯 Interview Q:** Interface aur Type me kya farq hai?
- **Interface**: Object ka shape define karta hai. `extends` se inherit ho sakta hai.
- **Type**: Kuch bhi define kar sakta hai (union, intersection, primitives).
- Interface ko merge kar sakte ho (same naam se dobara declare karke).

