### 4️⃣ [middlewares/trycatch.ts](file:///c:/Users/rajni/mobigo/services/auth/src/middlewares/trycatch.ts) — Error Wrapper 🛡️

```typescript
import { Request, Response, RequestHandler, NextFunction } from "express";
// ^ Express ke built-in types import kiye

const TryCatch = (handler: RequestHandler): RequestHandler => {
// ^ TryCatch ek HIGHER-ORDER FUNCTION hai
// Higher-Order Function = Jo function ko argument me le ya function return kare
//
// handler: RequestHandler → Ye wo actual controller function hai
//                          (jaise loginUser, addUserRole)
// : RequestHandler → Return bhi ek RequestHandler type ka function hoga

    return async (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {
    // ^ Ek naya function RETURN kar rahe hain jo original handler ko
    //   try-catch me wrap kar deta hai!

        try {
            await handler(req, res, next);
            // ^ Original controller function ko call karo
            // Agar sab theek raha toh normally response chala jayega
        } catch(err: any) {
            // ^ Agar controller me koi bhi error aaya (DB fail, etc.)
            // toh yahan pakad liya jayega
            res.status(500).json({
                message: err.message
                // Client ko error message bhej do
            });
        }
    }
}
export default TryCatch;
```

**💡 Ye kyu banaya?**
Bina TryCatch ke, har controller me manually try-catch likhna padta:
```typescript
// ❌ Bina TryCatch ke (Repetitive Code):
export const loginUser = async (req, res) => {
    try {
        // ... 20 lines of logic
    } catch(err) {
        res.status(500).json({ message: err.message });
    }
}
export const addUserRole = async (req, res) => {
    try {
        // ... 20 lines of logic
    } catch(err) {
        res.status(500).json({ message: err.message }); // Same code repeat!
    }
}

// ✅ TryCatch ke saath (DRY - Don't Repeat Yourself):
export const loginUser = TryCatch(async (req, res) => {
    // ... sirf logic likho, try-catch ki tension nahi!
});
```

